      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McBride%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Stephan McBride, the family’s patriarch, arrived in Perry County in 1837, leading the first settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McBride%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town blossomed along the Frisco Railway, complete with its own depot that once buzzed with travelers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McBride%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Great Flood of 1993 swept through McBride, destroying much of the community and reshaping its landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McBride%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Today, McBride hosts the Gilster‑Mary Lee Popcorn and Cereal plant, a local staple of snack production.",
